> Actually there is another PR : #14228
> 
> That would permit to create an opencode plugin for jdtls with lombok or add support for other lsp servers that are not build-in.
> 
> I think this PR, while being simpler for new comers, is not providing the level of extensibility the other one does. I think it would be better for everyone if #14228 was merged and someone provides a plugin for it.

I agree that this PR is simpler and not that powerful as plugin approach.
I do not have time to regularly update PR and I do not believe that plugins is much better solution unless plugin would also allow users to fine tune settings via nice UI experience.

For my needs I have downloaded lombok jar into `~/.config/opencode/` directory 
and changed ~/.config/opencode/opencode.jsonc so that it includes something like this (replace USER_HOME_DIR with your location):

```
  "lsp": {
    "jdtls": {
      "command": [
        "jdtls"
      ],
      "env": {
        "JAVA_TOOL_OPTIONS": "-javaagent:/USER_HOME_DIR/.config/opencode/lombok.jar"
      }
    }
  },
```

Because of the reasons stated above, I'm going to close this PR. If someone needs the idea - they will hopefully find issue and by that time there will be some working and robust solution.

## Workaround

The qwen models (`qwen3.6-plus`, `qwen3.5-plus`) are currently marked as `"status": "deprecated"` in the [models.dev](https://models.dev) registry that opencode pulls from. The provider loading code in `provider.ts` silently removes any model with that status, which is why they disappear even when your API key is valid.

You can override the status in your `opencode.jsonc` config by adding `"status": "beta"` to each qwen model entry (note: `"active"` is not a valid schema value and `"alpha"` is also hidden unless `OPENCODE_ENABLE_EXPERIMENTAL_MODELS` is set — `"beta"` is the only value that passes the filter):

```jsonc
"provider": {
  "opencode-go": {
    "models": {
      "qwen3.6-plus": {
        "name": "Qwen3.6 Plus",
        "reasoning": true,
        "status": "beta",
      },
      "qwen3.5-plus": {
        "name": "Qwen3.5 Plus",
        "reasoning": true,
        "status": "beta",
      },
    },
  },
}
```

After saving, the models will appear in the list and work normally.

The underlying fix would be to either un-deprecate these models in models.dev, or to make the `deprecated` filter not apply to models that are explicitly re-enabled in user config.
